  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round1_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B027",
        "laureates": [
          "Christopher Jarzynski",
          "Denis J. Evans",
          "Gavin E. Crooks"
        ],
        "citation": "for fluctuation theorems revealing exact universal relations in nonequilibrium physics"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B003",
    "B035"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B027 remains my preference. The fluctuation theorems identify a clean and unexpectedly universal mechanism linking microscopic reversibility, work fluctuations, and irreversible behavior. Evans, Jarzynski, and Crooks represent a coherent chain from the original relation to broadly applicable formulations. The relations are both theoretically secure and tested across controlled mesoscopic, molecular, and soft-matter systems, giving this conceptual discovery unusual breadth and maturity.",
    "case_against": "Its strongest reservation is that the achievement is a framework of closely related theorems rather than one singular experimental discovery, and the historical priority among formulations must be specified carefully. Experimental tests also differ substantially in idealization and control.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson places B013 first because atomic quantum information and simulation combine foundational architectures with decades of highly controlled experimental realization.",
        "response": "I agree that B013 is a formidable candidate and that its experimental control is exceptional. Yet its credit boundary overlaps trapped-ion, optical-lattice, and broader quantum-information programmes. B027 is more sharply delimited as a physical discovery: a general exact structure for nonequilibrium fluctuations, with a compact and historically intelligible attribution."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson argues that B003 transformed the quantitative treatment of strongly correlated materials and is a durable foundation of correlated-electron theory.",
        "response": "I share the high assessment of B003 and retain it as an alternative. Its practical and intellectual influence is undeniable, but its foundational development and later ecosystem are distributed across a substantial community. For B027, the essential mechanism and the distinct contributions of the three proposed laureates are presently more readily bounded."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll emphasizes that B035 has achieved reproducible, extraordinary precision and supports both fundamental tests and broad metrological uses.",
        "response": "The maturity and attribution case for B035 are excellent. I would nevertheless distinguish a remarkably successful precision platform from B027's discovery of a universal law-like relation extending thermodynamics into nonequilibrium small systems. The latter has the more fundamental conceptual unity for my preference."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the prize citation should emphasize the original Evans fluctuation relation or the later Jarzynski and Crooks work relations.",
      "Whether the experimental record is sufficiently decisive to overcome the absence of one defining macroscopic discovery."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No recusal-triggering connection is apparent from the supplied profile. It notes that Göran Johansson and Eva Olsson work in the linked Gothenburg physics environment, but identifies no specific collaboration."
  }
}
